Description: WWAN Linux services for Rolling Wireless modem modules
 This package provides the userspace services used to manage Rolling
 Wireless WWAN modules on Linux:
 .
  * rolling_helper - D-Bus API broker for the other services
  * rolling_config - OEM and module configuration service
  * rolling_flash  - firmware update / switch / recovery service
  * rolling_ma     - ModemManager FCC unlock helper
 .
 The services are shipped as systemd units and communicate over the system
 D-Bus.  The firmware images themselves are not part of this package; they
 are supplied separately by the OEM.
 .
 One binary package is produced per (project, OEM) pair, because the helper
 service and the configuration defaults differ between them.  Select the pair
 at build time through debian/rules; see debian/README.Debian.
 .
 ModemManager is required at runtime; fwupd is recommended because the
 firmware update path uses its fastboot plugin.
